cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "Infinite cycles in the interchange process in five dimensions: a Lean 4 formalization of Elboim and Sly"
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/scottnarmstrong/elboim-sly"
abstract: >-
  A machine-checked Lean 4 and Mathlib formalization of D. Elboim and A. Sly,
  Infinite cycles in the interchange process in five dimensions
  (arXiv:2211.17023). For d >= 5 and beta large, the interchange permutation
  pi_beta of Z^d almost surely has an infinite cycle, and the cycle of the
  origin is finite with probability less than 2/beta. The multiscale induction
  (Theorem 3.2) and every result of the paper it depends on are proved, together
  with every cited input: Poisson point processes, the construction of the
  process on the infinite lattice, the zero-one law, random walk and Brownian
  motion estimates, and strong approximations replacing Zaitsev's
  multidimensional KMT theorem. The library contains no sorry and no custom
  axiom.
authors:
  - family-names: Armstrong
    given-names: Scott
  - family-names: Bou-Rabee
    given-names: Ahmed
keywords:
  - Lean
  - mathlib
  - formal verification
  - probability
  - interchange process
  - random stirring
  - infinite cycles
  - strong approximation
license: Apache-2.0
